    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d201-a2">

                <pb facs="0373" n="301" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg301"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 256.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoppin to Lord Granville.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-09-28"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 28,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: Referring to my note of the 22d
                    instant, to which I have not yet had the pleasure of a reply, I trust your
                    lordship will pardon me if I repeat the request therein contained, that I may be
                    informed whether William Brophy, an American suspect, detained under the
                    protection of person and property (Ireland) act, and whose release from prison
                    is said to have been announced in the newspapers, has been really discharged. I
                    have been requested by telegram from the Department of State at Washington to
                    ascertain the facts in this case.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>W. J. HOPPIN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
